        "category": "Food Preservation • Methods & Principles",
        "q": "Explain three traditional methods of preserving food at home. How do they prevent food spoilage?",
        "ans": "<strong>Three Traditional Preservation Methods:</strong><br>\n1. <strong>Sun-Drying (Dehydration):</strong> Removing all moisture content from foods by spreading them in strong sunlight. Without moisture, bacteria and fungi cannot grow. <em>Examples:</em> Raw mango slices (amchur), red chillies, papads.<br>\n2. <strong>Pickling in Salt &amp; Mustard Oil:</strong> High salt draws out water from microbial cells (osmosis), and an oil layer on top blocks contact with airborne oxygen, preventing bacterial multiplication. <em>Examples:</em> Mango, lemon, and amla pickles.<br>\n3. <strong>Sugar Syrupping:</strong> Storing boiled fruits in thick, concentrated sugar syrup where microbes cannot survive due to high osmotic pressure. <em>Examples:</em> Murabba, fruit jams.",
        "marks": 3,
